{
  "about": "The W over P rows of the pico ABI performance matrix (docs/pico-perf-matrix.md section 5, docs/upstream-parity.md D9), judged by `scripts/host-bench/perf_matrix.py --gate` after every run of `scripts/pico-compare.sh perf`. A row is the cost ratio of one held figure of one cell (wz's over zenoh-pico's for a figure better lower, the reverse for one better higher; below 1 is wz ahead): {\"locked\": true} holds the cell to WIN, {\"ratio_at_most\": R} holds the upper end of its bootstrap interval to R times one plus `tolerance`, {\"reference_lost\": WHY} records a cell the reference lost every repetition of, and null is not filled yet, a failure whose sentence prints the row a run writes. The rows are the population of the default matrix (`--check-table`); a row is written only from the gate's own output for a run, never by hand.",
